  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- 17 fixture classes each start their own Testcontainers Postgres container,
         and xUnit parallelizes collections (one per class), so they start together.
         That used to surface as Npgsql "Connection reset by peer" — NOT a test-logic
         bug and NOT contention: `pg_isready` without `-h` probes the container's
         internal Unix socket, which greens while the entrypoint's temporary
         `listen_addresses=''` server is still bootstrapping and nothing is listening
         on 5432 yet. Collection serialization was the original mitigation and never
         eliminated it; the probe fix (`-h 127.0.0.1`, in every fixture) did.
         `parallelizeTestCollections` is therefore back to `true` — measured 262/262
         over six consecutive runs at ~33s versus ~79s serialized. Do not re-serialize
         without a measurement; see fix-testcontainers-tcp-readiness design D4. -->
    <None Include="xunit.runner.json" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" />
  </ItemGroup>

